---
import CodeStepper from "../../components/CodeStepper.astro";
import LessonLayout from "../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro";
import { algorithms, variables } from "../../lessons/circular-queues/lesson";
import { pageUrl } from "../../lib/links";
---

<LessonLayout
  title="Circular queues | A Level Computer Science"
  description="Learn how a circular queue works in Python, one line at a time, for Cambridge International A Level Computer Science (9618)."
>
  <main class="page">
    <p class="crumb"><a href={pageUrl()}>Cambridge A Level Computer Science (9618)</a> / Abstract data types</p>
    <h1 class="lesson-title">Circular queues</h1>
    <div class="prose lesson-intro">
      <p class="lesson-lead">A circular queue reuses the space at the front of the array.</p>
      <p>
        In a <a href={pageUrl("lessons/queues")}>linear queue</a>, the pointers only move forwards, so the queue can report full while the front of the array is empty.
        A circular queue fixes this: when a pointer goes past the end of the array, it wraps round to index 0.
      </p>
      <p>
        The code is almost the same as the linear queue. <code>HeadPointer</code> holds the index of the front item, <code>TailPointer</code> marks the back, and <code>NumberItems</code> counts the items.
        There are two differences. After each pointer moves, an <code>if</code> sends it back to 0 at the end of the array. And because <code>TailPointer</code> can wrap round, the queue is full when <code>NumberItems</code> equals <code>QueueSize</code>, not when <code>TailPointer</code> reaches the end.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="lesson-section">
      <h2>Watch the code run</h2>
      <p class="prose">
        Select <strong>Next line</strong> to run the code one line at a time. The yellow line has just run. The pink arrow shows <code>TailPointer</code>, and the green arrow shows <code>HeadPointer</code>. Start with <strong>Tail wraps round</strong> to see the linear queue's problem fixed.
      </p>
      <CodeStepper algorithms={algorithms} visual="circular-queue" variables={variables} />
    </section>
  </main>
</LessonLayout>
